+# Host-native boundary inventory
+
+`check_boundary.py` is a source-only checkpoint tool for the first host-native
+AMDGPU extraction step. It lists the existing GPU/Vega and host-protocol files
+that can be reused, and the current files that still require an x86 CPU,
+`ThreadContext`, an SE `Process`, or x86 page-table types.
+
+Run it from any directory with:
+
+```sh
+python3 util/host_native/check_boundary.py
+python3 util/host_native/check_boundary.py --check
+```
+
+The JSON output is deterministic and contains source markers and evidence
+locations. `--check` reports a failure only when a declared file or marker is
+missing, or when the inventory schema is malformed. It does not compile or
+run gem5.
+
+The inventory intentionally makes no claim about a host-native build, an
+x86-free binary, simulator execution, Triton compilation, or an end-to-end
+`python/tutorials/01-vector-add.py` run. The existing `configs/example/apu_se.py`
+`VEGA_X86` path remains the compatibility path until those later gates pass.
